CORE
main.ii
--winx64 --cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assignability: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
MSVC's __is_assignable_no_precondition_check was not a keyword in Visual
Studio mode; as an unknown function its call made every use false, so
std::pair's copy assignment was not viable and the deleted volatile one
was chosen ("is not accessible", cpp11_range_for_variable_scope).
